n style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;502,973&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;&#8212;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%"&gt;&#8212;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:1.5pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;___________&lt;br/&gt;(a) Includes $224.2 million and $220.6 million, as of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025, respectively, held in exchange traded funds with underlying investments in debt securities that meet the definition of equity securities with readily determinable fair values.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;There were no purchases, sales, issuances and settlements related to the assets in the Level 3 fair value measurement category during the six months ended June 30, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;F. &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Employee Benefits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Contributions from EPE to the Retirement Income Plan ("Retirement Plan") and the Other Postretirement Benefit Plan ("OPEB Plan") are based on various factors, such as the minimum funding amounts required by the U.S. Internal Revenue Service, state and federal regulatory requirements, amounts requested from customers in EPE's Texas and New Mexico jurisdictions, and the projected annual net periodic benefit cost of the Retirement Plan and OPEB Plan, as actuarially calculated. EPE projected $7.5 million and $1.2 million in 2026 annual contributions for its Retirement Plan and OPEB Plan, respectively. During the three months and six months ended June 30, 2026, EPE contributed $4.5 million and $4.5 million to its Retirement Plan and $0.6 million and $0.6 million to its OPEB Plan, respectively. During the three months and six months ended June 30, 2025, EPE contributed $3.0 million and $6.0 million to its Retirement Plan and $0.3 million and $0.6 million to its OPEB Plan, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;G.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Long-Term Debt, Financing Obligations and Capital Lease Obligations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;$150.0 million Term Loan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On January 16, 2025, EPE issued $150.0 million Term Loan Agreement with a maturity date of January 15, 2026. The interest rate of the $150.0 million term loan is equal to the greatest of (a) the Prime Rate in effect on such day, (b) the Federal Funds Rate in effect on such day plus one half of one percent (0.5%) and (c) Adjusted Term on the Secured Overnight Financing Rate ("SOFR") for one-month tenor in effect on such day plus one percent (1.0%). On January 15, 2026, EPE repaid the $150.0 million term loan at maturity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;$300 million Senior Notes. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On May 12, 2026, EPE issued 5.58% and 6.29% Senior Unsecured Notes with aggregate principal amounts of $80.0 million and $220.0 million, respectively, with maturity dates of May 12, 2036 and May 12, 2056, respectively. EPE typically uses the proceeds from the sale of senior notes for the repayment of existing indebtedness and for general corporate purposes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;See Note G of the Notes to Financial Statements in the 2025 FERC Form No. 1 for further discussion of EPE&#8217;s long-term debt, financing obligations and capital lease obligations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;H. &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Equity Contributions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Equity Contributions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;. On March 19, 2026 and April 1, 2026, Sun Jupiter Holdings, LLC, parent company of EPE ("Parent") made equity contributions to EPE in the amounts of $50.0 million and $215.0 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:139%"&gt;I. &#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Dividends. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;On July 28, 2026, EPE&#8217;s Board of Directors declared a quarterly cash dividend to Parent in the amount of $66.4 million, which was paid on July 31, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;Equity Contributions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;. On July 6, 2026, August 3, 2026, and August 7, 2026, Parent made equity contributions to EPE in the amounts of $100.0 million, $100.0 million, and $77.8 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:9pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:22.5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:139%"&gt;EPE has evaluated subsequent events through August 12, 2026, the date at which the financial statements were available to be issued, and determined there are no other items to disclose.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
