  <ferc:VendorName id="f-2917" contextRef="c-1">The Workiva Platform</ferc:VendorName>
  <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-1" id="fn-1" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In accordance with the FERC Guidance Letter AI07-1-000 related to FASB guidance for employers' accounting for defined benefit pension and other postretirement plans, this amount includes reclassification adjustments of accumulated other comprehensive income as a result of gains or losses, prior service costs or credits and transition assets or obligations related to pension and other postretirement benefit plans.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:6pt;text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">During the first quarter of 2005, EPE entered into treasury rate lock agreements to hedge against potential movements in the treasury reference interest rate pending the issuance of 6% Senior Notes. These treasury rate locks were terminated on May 11, 2005. The treasury rate lock agreements met the criteria for hedge accounting and were designated as a cash flow hedge. In accordance with cash flow hedge accounting, EPE recorded the loss associated with the fair value of the cash flow hedge of approximately $14.5 million, net of tax, as a component of accumulated other comprehensive income. Beginning in May 2005, and through May 2035, EPE will recognize in earnings (as additional interest expense) the accumulated other comprehensive income associated with the cash flow hedge. During the next twelve-month period, approximately $1.0 million pre-tax of this accumulated other comprehensive income item will be reclassified to interest expense.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Total Electric Plant in Service excludes Property Held for Future Development of $7,098,784.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">This item relates to (i) the regulatory treatment of the equity portion of AFUDC which is recovered in rate base by an offset with the related accumulated deferred income tax liability, and (ii) excess deferred state income taxes which are recovered through amortization to tax expense in cost of service. The amortization period for the excess deferred state income taxes is 15 years as established in the PUCT Final Order in Docket No. 44941 and the NMPRC Final Order in Case No. 15-00127-UT ("NMPRC Case No. 15-00127 Final Order").</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Amortization is based on a pro rata relationship with nuclear fuel amortization.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:3pt;text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Final coal mine reclamation costs are related to EPE's previous ownership interest in the Four Corners Generation Station ("Four Corners"), and represent the cost to reclaim the land disturbed during the coal mining that was not previously reclaimed while the mine was in operation.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:3pt;text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Pursuant to the final order in NMPRC Case No. 15-00109-UT, the New Mexico jurisdiction portion of the final coal reclamation costs are to be recovered through the Fuel and Purchase Power Cost Adjustment Clause ("FPPCAC") over a seven-year period beginning with the rate case to be filed after closing the sale of EPE's interest in Four Corners on July 6, 2016.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In accordance with the order in Case No. 15-00109-UT, EPE requested recovery of the final coal reclamation costs in its 2020 New Mexico rate case filing, Case No. 20-00104-UT. On June 23, 2021, the NMPRC issued its final order in the 2020 New Mexico Rate Case, which did not alter EPE&#8217;s request for recovery of the coal reclamation costs. The seven-year recovery period for the coal reclamation costs began in July 2021.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-bottom:3pt;text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">The NMPRC in Case No. 15-00109-UT approved EPE's request for an accounting order establishing $1.4 million of costs related to the decommissioning of Four Corners as a regulatory asset to be recovered over a seven-year period beginning in the rate case to be filed after closing the sale of EPE's interest in Four Corners on July 6, 2016. The recovery was requested in EPE's 2020 New Mexico rate case filing, Case No. 20-00104-UT. On June 23, 2021, the NMPRC issued its final order in the 2020 New Mexico Rate Case, which approved EPE&#8217;s request for recovery of decommissioning costs. The seven-year recovery period for decommissioning costs began in July 2021.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents rate case costs incurred after August 1, 2017 related to EPE's 2017 rate case, Docket No. 46831. In accordance with the Final Order in Docket No. 46831, EPE requested recovery of these costs in EPE's 2021 Texas base rate case filing, Docket No. 52195 ("2021 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing"). On September 15, 2022, the PUCT issued the PUCT Final Order in Docket No. 52195 ("2021 PUCT Final Order") which allowed recovery of these costs over a four-year recovery period which began in August 2022.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's 2021 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing in PUCT Docket No. 52195. The 2021 PUCT Final Order approved the recovery of rate case expenses incurred before April 1, 2022 over a four-year recovery period which began in August 2022. Costs incurred after April 2022 were approved for recovery in EPE&#8217;s 2025 Texas base rate case filing, Docket No. 57568 (&#8220;2025 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing&#8221;). On April 2, 2026, the PUCT issued the PUCT Final order in Docket No. 57568 (&#8220;2025 PUCT Final Order&#8221;) which allowed recovery of these costs over a two-year recovery period which began in April 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE&#8217;s 2025 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing in PUCT Docket No. 57568. The 2025 PUCT Final Order approved the recovery of rate case expenses incurred before April 1, 2025 over a two-year period which began in April 2026. EPE will request recovery of costs incurred April 2025 and later in a future base rate case filing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">This item relates to a relate-back surcharge pursuant to the 2021 PUCT Final Order. Pursuant to the order, EPE is recovering a portion of the base rate increase for the period of November 3, 2021 through July 31, 2022 through a relate-back surcharge that is partially offset the corresponding excess deferred tax credits by customer class. The net excess deferred tax credits are being credited to customers over a four-year recovery period which began in August 2022.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Additionally, in the 2021 PUCT Final Order, a GCRR baseline was adopted which would allow recovery of Newman Unit 6 from Texas customers. EPE began billing approved GCRR rates on February 1, 2024, after COD of Newman Unit 6. On January 31, 2025, the PUCT adopted EPE's proposed updated rate in Docket No. 56225 which reflects the Texas jurisdictional portion of the full cost for Newman Unit 6 from its Texas customers. EPE began billing the interim rate on May 1, 2024.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's filing for its voluntary business solar program for its Texas jurisdiction with the PUCT in Docket No. 55176. EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2025 Texas Retail Rate Case in PUCT Docket No. 57568. The 2025 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a two-year recovery period which began in April 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's filing for its Transportation Electrification Plan ("TEP"), including approval of four electric vehicle-ready pilot programs and tariffs for its Texas jurisdiction with the PUCT in Docket No. 54614. EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2025 Texas Retail Rate Case in PUCT Docket No. 57568. The 2025 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a two-year recovery period which began in April 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's Advanced Metering System ("AMS") filing for its Texas jurisdiction with the PUCT in Docket No. 52040. EPE requested recovery of the filing costs in the 2021 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing, Docket No. 52195. The 2021 PUCT Final Order approved the recovery of costs incurred before April 1, 2022 over a four-year recovery period which began in August 2022. Costs incurred after April 2022 were requested for recovery in the 2025 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing in PUCT Docket No. 57568. The 2025 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a two-year recovery period which began in April 2026. The balance also includes an under-recovery of the AMS net revenue requirement through each corresponding year.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's filing to establish its Transmission Cost Recovery Factor ("TCRF") with the PUCT in Docket No. 49148. EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2021 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing. The 2021 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a four-year recovery period which began in August 2022.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's filing to establish its Distribution Cost Recovery Factor ("DCRF") with the PUCT in Docket No. 49395. EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2021 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing. The 2021 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a four-year recovery period which began in August 2022.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents filing costs related to the 2019 Texas Fuel Reconciliation Filing in PUCT Docket No. 50058. EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2021 Texas Retail Rate Case Filing. The 2021 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a four-year recovery period which began in August 2022.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents filing costs related to the 2022 Texas Fuel Reconciliation Filing in PUCT Docket No. 54142. EPE requested recovery of these costs in its 2025 Texas Retail Rate Case in PUCT Docket No. 57568. The 2025 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a two-year recovery period which began in April 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's filing to establish its GCRR related to Newman Unit 6 in PUCT Docket No. 54659. EPE requested recovery of these costs in its 2025 Texas Retail Rate Case in PUCT Docket No. 57568. The 2025 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a two-year recovery period which began in April 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents filing costs related to the 2024 Texas Fuel Reconciliation Filing in PUCT Docket No. 57149. EPE will request recovery of these costs in a future base rate case proceeding.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs related to EPE's filing of the Texas Transmission and Distribution Systems Resiliency Plan in PUCT Docket No. 59137. EPE will request recovery of these costs in a future base rate case proceeding.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's filing to establish its 2024 Texas DCRF with the PUCT in Docket No. 56425. EPE requested recovery of these costs in its 2025 Texas Retail Rate Case in PUCT Docket No. 57568. The 2025 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a two-year recovery period which began in April 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In NMPRC Case No.15-00127-UT, the NMPRC approved EPE's request to recover costs related to renewable energy certificates and procurement plan costs over a six-year period beginning July 1, 2016. EPE requested costs incurred after December 31, 2014 as a component of base rates in EPE's 2020 New Mexico rate case filing, Case No. 20-00104-UT. On June 23, 2021, the NMPRC issued its final order in the 2020 New Mexico rate case allowing recovery of these costs. Pursuant to the final order in Case No. 20-00104-UT, the recovery period for costs incurred prior to December 31, 2014 was extended five years beginning March 2021. The five-year recovery period for costs incurred after December 31, 2014 began in July 2021 and ended in June 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">EPE requested recovery of these costs in EPE's 2020 New Mexico rate case filing, Case No. 20-00104-UT. On June 23, 2021, the NMPRC issued its final order in the 2020 New Mexico rate case allowing recovery of these costs. The five-year recovery of these costs began in July 2021 and ended in June 2026..</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents filing costs associated with EPE's 2026 New Mexico Retail Rate Case filing in NMPRC Case No. 25-00082-UT. These costs were requested for recovery in this case.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-26" id="fn-26" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On February 22, 2017, the NMPRC approved, in Case No. 17-00016-UT, EPE's request to implement a Demand Response Pilot Program pursuant to its proposed Original Rate No. 37. This program provides an incentive for customers to switch to eSmart Thermostats, giving EPE the ability to slightly modify the eSmart Thermostats during peak times. Program costs incurred as of December 31, 2019 were requested in EPE's 2020 New Mexico Rate Case, Case No. 20-00104-UT. On June 23, 2021, the NMPRC issued its final order in the 2020 New Mexico rate case allowing recovery of these costs. The five-year recovery of these costs began in July 2021 and ended in June 2026.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-27" id="fn-27" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs associated with EPE's New Mexico Transportation Electrification Plan ("NMTEP") filed with the NMPRC in Case No. 20-00241-UT. The NMPRC approved EPE's request to recover costs related to the NMTEP, and EPE began recovering NMTEP costs effective March 2023 through a rider approved by the NMPRC through New Mexico Rate 44. The rate is updated annually.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-28" id="fn-28" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On November 2, 2022, the NMPRC approved, in Case No. 21-00269-UT, EPE's request to recover costs associated with EPE's AMS project for its New Mexico jurisdiction via a rider under New Mexico Rate 46. The balance includes an under-recovery of the AMS net revenue requirement through December of each corresponding year. Filing costs associated with the New Mexico AMS project were requested in the 2026 New Mexico Retail Rate Case filed with the NMPRC in Case No. 25-00082-UT.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-29" id="fn-29" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On September 15, 2021 the NMPRC granted, in Case No. 21-00180-UT, EPE's request to recover non-capitalized Western Energy Imbalance Market (''EIM'') implementation costs on a New Mexico jurisdictional basis. EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2026 New Mexico Retail Rate Case filed with the NMPRC in Case No. 25-00082-UT.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">On November 30, 2023, the NMPRC issued a Final Order on Remand to the NMPRC Case No. 20-00104-UT, which approved EPE&#8217;s updated filed rates effective January 1, 2024. The updated rates include approximately $0.6 million in additional annual base revenue requirement related to amounts found to be unlawfully excluded by the NMPRC's prior order in the case. The Final Order on Remand also approved EPE's request to record additional revenue from the date of the Supreme Court remand to December 31, 2023, as a regulatory asset for recovery in EPE&#8217;s next rate case.&#160;&#160;EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2026 New Mexico Retail Rate Case filed with the NMPRC in Case No. 25-00082-UT.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents New Mexico portion of Buena Vista Battery capacity charges that were approved by the NMPRC in Case No. 19-00348-UT as a system resource. EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2026 New Mexico Retail Rate Case filed with the NMPRC in Case No. 25-00082-UT.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs related to the New Mexico AMS Time Varying Rate Pilot Program in NMPRC Case No. 24-00113-UT. EPE requested recovery of these costs in the 2026 New Mexico Retail Rate Case filed with the NMPRC in Case No. 25-00082-UT.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs related to the New Mexico Community Solar Program for solar bill credits and administrative costs as authorized in NMPRC Case No. 23-00071-UT. EPE will request recovery of these costs in a future base rate case proceeding.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs related to the external audit of EPE's FPPCAC filing in accordance with NMPRC Case No. 23-00046-UT. EPE will request recovery of these costs in a future base rate case proceeding.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Represents costs incurred for the FERC transmission rate case for its FERC jurisdiction. EPE requested these costs in its FERC rate case filing in Docket No. ER22-282-000. The 2024 FERC Final Order allowed recovery of these costs over a three-year period which began in August 2024.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In NMPRC Case No. 09-00171-UT, the NMPRC extended the depreciable life of Palo Verde an additional 20 years for New Mexico rate making purposes, reducing the depreciation expense collected from New Mexico customers in rates, effective January 2010. In April 2011, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission renewed the operating license for all three units at Palo Verde for an additional 20 years; therefore, the incremental difference in Palo Verde depreciation for the New Mexico jurisdiction is being amortized to account 407.3 over the remaining life of Palo Verde.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%">In March 2020, the PUCT authorized utility companies to defer and recover COVID-19 related costs. The 2021 PUCT Final Order allowed recovery of $6.3 million in deferred COVID-19 costs incurred through December 31, 2020, over a four-year recovery period which began in August 2022, and also required the filing of annual COVID-related cost true-ups each March. In March 2024, EPE filed its second annual update filing with the PUCT in Docket No. 56422 which included a net amount of $8.5 million in COVID-19 related costs for the four years 2020 to 2023 on a Texas jurisdictional basis for bad debt and other expenses related to COVID-19, after the reduction of revenues collected through the rider. The parties agreed to a stipulation in the case which was approved by the PUCT on October 2, 2025, resulting in a revised net amount of $7.2 million. The COVID-19 Rider will recover $2.0 million annually until July 2028.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">As of June 30, 2026, EPE has recorded $4.0 million as a regulatory asset and $0.7 million as a regulatory liability related to the New Mexico portion of COVID-related costs and potential savings. EPE requested recovery of the net amount in the 2026 New Mexico Retail Rate Case filed with the NMPRC in Case No. 25-00082-UT. These balances were fully reserved, with no net effect on the financial statements.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">This item primarily relates to the reduction in the federal corporate income tax rate from 35% to 21% as enacted by the TCJA. The amortization period for the excess TCJA portion is based on the average rate assumption method for protected assets in both jurisdictions, Texas and New Mexico, in accordance with the 2021 PUCT Final Order and the 2020 NMPRC Final Order.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In accordance with the final order in PUCT Docket No. 37690, EPE began recovering Energy Efficiency Program costs through a tariff rider approved by the PUCT via Texas Rate 97, effective July 2010. The rate is updated annually.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-40" id="fn-40" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">In accordance with the final order in NMPRC Case No. 06-00065-UT, EPE started collecting Energy Efficiency costs, effective May 2009, through a tariff rider approved by the NMPRC via New Mexico Rate 17. The rate is updated annually.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Below is the detail of Miscellaneous Service Revenues recorded in account 451:</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
